    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Your phone, programmable</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">ZetaForge runs plugins: real programs, written by you or by someone you trust, that do things on this device. No store, no account.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_trust_title">A plugin is not an app in a box</string>
    <string name="onboarding_trust_body">A plugin runs inside ZetaForge, with the permissions you grant to ZetaForge. It is not sandboxed. Installing one is as consequential as installing an app — so only import packages you trust.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_trust_point_source">You can read the source of any plugin, right here in the app.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_trust_point_permissions">Every permission is asked for with a reason, every time it runs.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_trust_point_stop">Any run can be stopped from its notification.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_schedule_title">It can work while you don’t</string>
    <string name="onboarding_schedule_body">Plugins can run on a schedule — nightly, hourly, only while charging — and keep going with the screen off. Android needs two things from you for that to be reliable.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_ready_title">You’re set</string>
    <string name="onboarding_ready_body">Import a .zeta package to get started. You can change any of this later from the menu.</string>

